[
  {
    "name": "list-read: a flat to-do list body decodes into the todolist shape",
    "description": "GET /todolists/{id} answers with the recordable's flat JSON. Before #544 the spec modelled the response as a oneOf envelope, and every SDK worked around it: Go and TypeScript re-decoded the raw body by hand, Kotlin received an untyped JsonElement, and Swift's SYNTHESISED two-arm Codable decoded the flat body into two nil members and reported success — #574 later replaced that with a hand-written flat-body fallback plus an arm-masking guard, so the nil-members failure is the origin of this work rather than the state it lands on. What survived to this change is narrower and still lossy: the todolist arm modelled no group_position_url, color or comments_app_url at all, so a group read silently dropped its group-position URL. This case pins the decode through the SDK's own model: the responseBody assertions read the re-serialized result, so a decoder that yields nothing fails here rather than silently returning it. groups_url is present because this recording's parent is a Todoset.",
